# Post-generation music evaluation

**When:** After any music generation succeeds (MIDI written). Skip if code-only
edits with no new MIDI.

## 1. Objective (always try first)

Run MusPy via:

```text
py -3 prttype/evaluate_midi.py <path.mid> --key <KEY> --mode <MODE>
```

Or rely on `generate_from_prompt.py` (default `--eval`; disable with `--no-eval`).

Report M1–M4 from the script. These are **person-independent** validity checks,
not aesthetic quality. M5 (OA/KLD) needs a reference corpus — skip unless asked.

## 2. Subjective (ask the user)

Ask for **Q1–Q4 + O1** on a **1–5** scale (do not invent scores):

| ID | Axis | Definition |
|----|------|------------|
| Q1 | Melodiousness | 旋律として音楽的・調和的に聞こえるか |
| Q2 | Rhythmicity | 拍・リズムにまとまりがあるか |
| Q3 | Structureness | 反復や展開など、構造的なまとまりがあるか |
| Q4 | Correctness | 突然の無音・不自然な飛びなど、技術的破綻が少ないか |
| O1 | Overall | 総合的に、この曲の聴感品質に満足できるか |

## 3. Summary

Short table: MusPy numbers + user scores. If any Qi/O1 ≤ 2, one-line next fix.

Do **not** use SongEval axes or Chu Creativity / Richness / Naturalness / Coherence
unless the user asks.

